# Proof, Information, and Heat: An Interactive Path

A proof may be concise while its discovery is expensive. This notebook separates the size of a description, the number of candidates searched, and the information erased by a physical process. Start with the [Landauer principle](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Landauer%27s_principle) and [Kolmogorov complexity](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kolmogorov_complexity), then explore the numerical consequences below.

## 1. Turn information into a thermodynamic scale

The benchmark $C_T(\pi)=T\ln(2)K(\pi)$ is linear in shortest-description complexity. It describes the ideal scale for erasing those description bits; it is not a universal meter of search energy.

