</details>

## 2. See why most objects are incompressible

In a prefix-free language, fewer than $2^m$ objects can have descriptions shorter than $m$ bits. Among $2^n$ distinct objects, more than a fraction $1-2^{-c}$ therefore require at least $n-c$ bits.

