</details>

## 3. Separate descriptions from search

A typical uniformly indexed object has a description of order $n$, but all binary candidates through length $n$ number $2^{n+1}-1$. Explore this gap and consult the [theory of computational complexity](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computational_complexity_theory) for broader resource measures.

