If every object in a $2^n$-member family has an $n$-bit index plus fixed decoding overhead, every complexity is at most $n+O(1)$. Incompressibility supplies a matching linear lower bound for the mean. The exponential number counts candidates in exhaustive search, not bits in a typical description.
</details>

## 4. Use sorting as the exact laboratory

Sorting $n$ distinct objects merges $n!$ possible input orders into one visible ordered output. The same factorial governs decision depth, erased information, and the history capacity needed for reversibility.

