</details>

## 5. What to measure next

For reasoning systems and learned models, report description size, search effort, verifier work, memory retained for reversibility, and actual device energy separately. The [reversible computing](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reversible_computing) perspective asks how much history must be preserved to avoid logical erasure. The next research target is a quantitative frontier relating verifier-fiber multiplicity, ancillary memory, and dissipated heat.
